Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["SortBibliography", "ObjectName",
 CellID->35156457,ExpressionUUID->"eca8cb0b-3623-25f8-7353-9dbbc4283982"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"6aac65c2-a8df-798f-03bc-23d2026a7a5f"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["SortBibliography",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/SortBibliography"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5b3fd7d9-846c-bdc8-5080-686dd489c28c"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "reorders the bibliography of the input notebook by the order of first citation, as BibTeX's unsrt does, moving the \\begin and \\end of the thebibliography to whichever entries become first and last.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["SortBibliography",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/SortBibliography"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "\"\<method\>\"", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "177c2e3e-8b0c-a8da-d3fc-04686a186309"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "orders the input notebook's bibliography: \"FirstUse\", \"Key\", \"Entry\" alphabetically on the entry text, or \"Uncited\", which sorts nothing and reports the entries no citation points at together with the citations pointing at no cell.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["SortBibliography",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/SortBibliography"], 
   RowBox[{"[", "notebook", "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "488da637-1710-a83f-1223-9d8b376e935e"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "orders the given ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["notebook", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "561b2c98-6218-5110-862d-d1833a47f4fd"],
 " by first use.",
 "\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   ButtonBox["SortBibliography",
    BaseStyle->"Link",
    ButtonData->"paclet:WolframInstitute/MathNotebook/ref/SortBibliography"], 
   RowBox[{"[", 
    RowBox[{"notebook", ", ", " ", "\"\<method\>\""}], "]"}]}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "16ba56c0-c331-6fdd-ab0c-aa6d29599a4f"],
 " \[LineSeparator]",
 "orders it by the given ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["method", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "79a2d5f5-53e5-4c8d-5877-940fa0b47350"],
 ". Where the entries come from a .bib file the order shown is the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["notebook", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6d6f799b-6fb8-2d91-af85-2a204f0d918c"],
 "'s alone, that file and its bibliography style deciding the compiled one."
}], "Usage",
 CellID->714434991,ExpressionUUID->"9a04050b-7d59-f599-7130-b49f2524fad1"],

Cell["\<\
Acts on the input notebook, or on the notebook given, rewriting its \
bibliography in place.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"41e0cdba-f105-4e75-9fed-c97f7588090c"],

Cell["\<\
\"FirstUse\" is the order of first citation, as BibTeX's unsrt style \
produces, and is the default. \"Key\" and \"Entry\" order alphabetically on \
the citation key and on the entry text.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e3fd8251-f24f-484a-b181-d0f1f9d07919"],

Cell["\<\
\"Uncited\" sorts nothing. It reports the entries that no citation points at, \
together with the citations that point at no cell in the notebook, and \
returns both as an association.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e23e201d-7ccc-40fa-a497-67c7be962de4"],

Cell["\<\
In a bibliography written into the document the order of the entries is the \
order the compiled paper prints, so the \\begin and \\end of the \
thebibliography environment are moved to whichever entries become first and \
last.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"15586a30-59ac-4a09-b1c2-59f3b53e92c1"],

Cell["\<\
Where the entries come from a .bib file, the order shown is the notebook's \
alone: that file and its bibliography style decide the order the compiled \
paper prints.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4bc520a3-1c60-45be-be89-55392e98193a"]
}, Open  ]],

